    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name was transferred from Geneva, Switzerland, reflecting early settlers’ admiration for the European city.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geneva%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Geographically, Geneva sits at 32°34′46″N 84°33′2″W, placing it in the western part of Talbot County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geneva%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "U.S. Route 80 runs through Geneva, connecting the town north to Talbotton and west to Columbus.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geneva%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The newly built Fall Line Freeway passes through Geneva, leading east to Junction City and running concurrently with State Route 96.",
